# Every file in this plugin is checked out with LF line endings, whatever the
# cloning machine's core.autocrlf says.
#
# WHY: Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites every text
# file to CRLF on checkout, and `/plugin marketplace add` clones with git. The
# hooks are executed by `/bin/sh` and `/usr/bin/env python3`, and a CRLF on their
# first line makes both fail before any code runs — `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M`
# (exit 127) and `env: python3\r: No such file or directory`. Measured on a copy
# of each hook with `\r` appended to every line, run the way hooks.json runs it.
#
# A path attribute beats the config setting, and git honours a .gitattributes
# inside a subdirectory for the paths beneath it — so this file travels with the
# plugin tree into the public repository and needs no copy at the root.
* text=auto eol=lf
hooks/* text eol=lf
# `bin/*` is named explicitly for the same reason `hooks/*` is, and it is
# not covered by the blanket line in the way it looks: `text=auto` leaves
# the text/binary decision to git's heuristic, and `bin/plexarm-headers`
# has no extension. A CRLF after `#!/bin/sh` is `bad interpreter:
# /bin/sh^M`, exit 127 — which the MCP client reports as `exec_failed`,
# and that path ends at an OAuth error naming neither the helper nor
# Plexarm. One line, and it is the cheapest control in the 1.7.0 change.
bin/* text eol=lf
